      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "King mackerel",
        "text_sha256": "6fe2a05b493a0d1d5314aea09477e046b4dc9e2f037079c37008c2e6d9c32503",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Marlin",
        "text_sha256": "6a6786c59c62c9ee2983ef565565fcd779791a9006d2e8f2e348572f637e5cd2",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Orange roughy",
        "text_sha256": "7ff4842904f4930e3964e9db0cd9aa0c5debb02a1977f14834227ec7606275df",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Shark",
        "text_sha256": "3565f8adfba6fc45e21baf44dbbd3454a04ff77c3d697c6bb5eefa7eca2db0af",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Swordfish",
        "text_sha256": "c6afd22545c477c9830ed96438a643317d6bbf38bb219df26ba837f3a10ecb99",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Tilefish from the Gulf of Mexico",
        "text_sha256": "ba54b5d3dafdb918d922f19de416599ba3cd939f5a7f82228754a149dc5c1d8d",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A number of other fish are safe to eat once per week, including Chilean sea bass, yellowfin tuna, striped ocean bass, mahi mahi, and halibut. See the full FDA and EPA list here .",
        "text_sha256": "8c9087c159c3c655e0e281d033658f9f6552d95a3bdd95b6e60319d5f46de94f",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Many What to Expect Community moms-to-be say they try to stick to these guidelines as much as possible. “I’ve laid off bigger saltwater fish (tuna, grouper, swordfish, seabass). But I eat salmon, shrimp, or scallops at least three or four times a week,” says pmm4204.",
        "text_sha256": "8cfd734072ed20a84c533ab68e2e845bdc9f3b9c2bc8ec89b16474cee345370d",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Having trouble remembering what's tame and what's toxic? In addition to the FDA and EPA's fish chart, the Monterey Bay Aquarium's Seafood Watch offers a handy, printable pocket-size list of fish and seafood that are good choices, good alternatives — or good to avoid (for a variety of reasons, including overfishing, damaged habitats, and pollutant levels).",
        "text_sha256": "bee63631b2eb66d175a7aca3ce96ea3411c1d0cea14282d1b8afb8cc703af789",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What if you're trying to get pregnant but you don't eat fish?",
        "text_sha256": "c5166b8dfc38266c5424761336c09e4752bc895251cb3af965a7fcff49162e90",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You may want to consider supplements. The omega-3 fatty acids found in fish and seafood are good not only for your heart, they're also great to prepare your body to grow healthy babies too. Studies show the oily omegas prevent preterm labor and preeclampsia while improving a baby's visual and cognitive functions.",
        "text_sha256": "e7a2e0ae71b457e49cc6df8c5e516ee478b0e5bbdaa5a9a98762cc28d8b754ba",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Some experts also believe that there's a connection between low DHA (omega-3's) and postpartum depression. But if you're not a fan of the fishy taste, you may be able to take fish oil capsules or a prenatal vitamin with omega-3's instead.",
        "text_sha256": "ae8c86c1736730c22b30dd521bdbe293e07d9f425526ac10b5d96736e8bd97aa",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000049",
        "block_index": 49,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "So if you're planning to conceive anytime soon, ask your healthcare provider for recommendations. Some prenatal vitamins now get their omega-3's from algae, an all-natural plant source of DHA, which makes them a great option for vegetarians. Another good option: DHA eggs, which are fortified with omega-3's from flaxseed fed to laying hens.",
        "text_sha256": "7f8fcef3b780382aae0e15f75bbba2e9472dd2899ced8354e69928982feaebeb",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000050",
        "block_index": 50,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "From TTC nutrition to daily support, the What to Expect app has you covered. Download it and start prepping for baby.",
        "text_sha256": "45c5ed44ded17f86579946d1e8c4bee9f8cca2730308cdda7ba2e110d08a69fa",
        "word_count": 21
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 850,
    "heading_count": 5
  },
